      "sequence_position": 11,
      "problem": "If $P$ is a statement, $\\text{t}$ is a tautology, and $\\text{c}$ is a contradiction, complete the following table of logical equivalences.\n\n| Statement | Is Logically Equivalent To |\n| --- | --- |\n| $\\text{c}∧\\text{t}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{c}∨\\text{t}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{t}∧¬P$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{t}∨P$ | {{field-4}} |",
      "worked_solution": "Recall the following properties of tautologies and contradictions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∨\\text{t}=\\text{t}\\, &  & A∧\\text{t} & =A \\\\ A∨\\text{c}=A\\, &  & A∧\\text{c} & =\\text{c} \\\\ \\text{t}∨\\text{t}=\\text{t}\\, &  & \\text{t}∧\\text{t} & =\\text{t} \\\\ \\text{t}∨\\text{c}=\\text{t}\\, &  & \\text{t}∧\\text{c} & =\\text{c} \\\\ \\text{c}∨\\text{t}=\\text{t}\\, &  & \\text{c}∧\\text{t} & =\\text{c} \\\\ \\text{c}∨\\text{c}=\\text{c}\\, &  & \\text{c}∧\\text{c} & =\\text{c}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe completed table is shown below.\n\n| Statement | Is Logically Equivalent To |\n| --- | --- |\n| $\\text{c}∧\\text{t}$ | $\\text{c}$ |\n| $\\text{c}∨\\text{t}$ | $\\text{t}$ |\n| $\\text{t}∧¬P$ | $¬P$ |\n| $\\text{t}∨P$ | $\\text{t}$ |",
